BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cc164b4f6b3fcb1d533308996cbe367a1ea450de@authenticatecon.com
DTSTAMP:20261012T182052Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T103000
SUMMARY:Member Plenary - Opening Plenary
LOCATION:Luna 1-2 (Members Only)\, Omni La Costa Resort & Spa\, 2100 Costa 
 Del Mar Rd\, Carlsbad\, CA 92009
DESCRIPTION:Opening Plenary\nAgenda:\n\n• State of the Alliance (20 minut
 es)\n• Update from Working Groups/Regional Working Groups (20 minutes)\n
 • Verifiable Digital Credentials for Singpass (20 minutes)\n• Speaker:
  Peng TIAN\, Engineering Manager\, Singpass GovTech Singapore\n• Abstrac
 t: Singpass is Singapore's national digital identity platform\, built on O
 penID Connect (OIDC)\, with a device-bound key pair in every user's app an
 d passkeys launching in 2026. But authentication only addresses online log
 ins. Identity also needs to be verified in the physical world — at count
 ers\, clinics\, hotels\, borders\, and even for deliveries — where ident
 ity presentation remains fragmented and potentially insecure. This led us 
 to explore Verifiable Digital Credentials (VDCs). This talk shares what we
  have learned so far\, including the challenges of taking VDCs from concep
 t towards national-scale deployment.\n\n• mDocs Beyond mDL - Cross-platf
 orm credentials for real-world use cases (20 minutes)\n• Speaker: Eran H
 aggiag\n• Abstract: mDocs have proven themselves for mobile driver's lic
 enses\, but the same data model can carry credentials for far more everyda
 y use cases. This session shares hands-on learnings from a pilot run at th
 e Global Digital Collaboration (GDC) Conference 2026 in Geneva\, where we 
 deployed a non-mDL mdoc across both Google Wallet and Apple Wallet using t
 he W3C Digital Credentials API — built and tested within months of the A
 PI reaching general availability in stable browsers. We deployed physical 
 readers for two real-world scenarios at the conference itself\, entrance c
 heck-in and a coffee station\, and had to reconcile the fact that Apple an
 d Android currently speak different protocol dialects under the same API s
 urface to get one credential working across both wallets. We'll walk throu
 gh what worked\, where that interoperability gap still bites\, and what ne
 eds to happen for this pattern to move from pilot to broad production use.
 \n\n• Workforce Credential Manager Certification Program Status (10 minu
 tes)\n• Speaker: Tim Cappalli\, Okta\nAgenda: https://authenticatecon.co
 m/event/authenticate-u-s-2026/
URL:https://authenticatecon.com/event/authenticate-u-s-2026/
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
